/**
 * headless-guard-and-truncate - Pi extension for unattended (print / json / rpc-without-UI) runs.
 *
 * Fixes two failure modes seen in Forge runs (docs/forge-lessons.md, 2026-10-16):
 *   1. A tool dumped a huge result (e.g. raw ComfyUI /object_info) and the 96K context window died silently.
 *   2. Unattended runs stalled or were refused on permission / [y/N] prompts.
 *
 * What it does
 *   - tool_call: static denylist for bash/powershell/write/edit. A block returns a TEXT reason to the model
 *     (no dialog), so the model can self-correct. Everything else passes silently.
 *   - tool_call (headless only, ALI-160 K4 2026-10-23): deny-by-default command allowlist for bash/powershell, read from
 *     headless-guard-allowlist.json next to this file. Runs after the denylist (which wins).
 *   - tool_result: any tool result over 32 KB or 1000 lines is spilled to %TEMP%\pi-tool-outputs\<uuid>.txt and
 *     replaced by the first 40 lines, the last 40 lines and the file path.
 *   - Headless only (ctx.hasUI === false): turns on pi-permission-system's runtime auto-approve (non-persistent)
 *     so `ask` rules stop blocking. `deny` rules and this denylist stay hard boundaries. Set
 *     PI_HEADLESS_GUARD_AUTO_APPROVE=0 to disable. Also exports non-interactive env defaults (git/pip).
 *
 * This is a best-effort static policy, not a sandbox. Pure helpers are exported for tests/headless-guard.test.mjs.
 */

